{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T11:22:56.337Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-jzrtsr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Platform nightly legs regress after the shell-dialect rendering: Windows tests expect POSIX recovery text, and macOS bash 3.2 with history expansion misparses a rendered command at a non-ASCII apostrophe"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The 2026-11-25 nightly (run 45629253836, commit b7356de67, the first main after the PowerShell and bash history-expansion rendering changes) failed on windows-latest shards 2, 3 and 4 and on macos-latest shard 1, so the aggregate ubuntu job failed too; the previous nightly on 6b998021d was green. Windows: recovery text is now rendered in the cmd dialect, for example ^\"command=^<actual command^>,timeout_seconds=\\^\"90\\^\"^\", while tests in linked-resource-admission.integration.spec.ts, linked-resource-recovery.spec.ts and register-commands.spec.ts expect the POSIX spelling command=<actual command>; these are platform-dependent expectations. macOS: rendered-command-shell-safety.integration.spec.ts 'posix: bash with history expansion on receives every argument literally' receives 25 arguments instead of 12, the parse breaking at the argument smart’s (U+2019), so a rendered command is not paste-safe under the system bash 3.2 with history expansion; this is a product defect, not only a test expectation. Linux passes both."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","macos","nightly","regression","shell","windows"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-26T11:22:56.337Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T11:22:56.337Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Windows recovery-text tests derive their expectations from the dialect renderer instead of a POSIX literal; The rendered-command safety test passes under bash 3.2 with history expansion, including non-ASCII arguments; A dispatched Nightly Validation run is green on every leg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":85},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Every nightly leg passes: Windows tests compare recovery text through the dialect renderer, and a rendered POSIX command survives bash 3.2 with history expansion byte for byte"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Windows legs fail on POSIX-spelled expectations and the macOS leg receives 25 arguments instead of 12 from one rendered command"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-kjoudp","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-26T11:22:56.337Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-oq893h","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-26T11:22:56.337Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9ca78a34c55b95efd0f5271396adcfc7645a2eaa21bd15e93fff574c90219608","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3a1cafe050a39f152bcd10e0842a74598114ada1c92c62c6af9245ab9368ceb0"}
