{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T14:36:44.653Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T14:36:44.653Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-26T14:36:44.652Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Root cause (macOS leg), reproduced in the official bash:3.2 image (3.2.57, same as macOS) and read in its lib/readline/histexpand.c and parse.y: history_expand first runs a quote tracker that, inside double quotes, skips the character after any backslash that precedes a double quote without pairing backslashes, so the rendered \\\\\" that ends a double-quoted argument with a trailing backslash (C:\\Program Files\\pm\\ in the fixture) leaves it inside double quotes; the later single-quoted '!bang!' then looks live and the expansion pass runs, and that pass breaks out of its loop after the first multibyte character (the U+2019 in smart’s), so the line is cut and bash reads the next physical line as the continuation of an open double quote: 12 arguments instead of 25. parse.y inhibits history expansion on a continuation line only inside a single-quoted string, so a double-quoted argument holding a line break is a second trigger (event not found, even without non-ASCII text); bash 5.3 handles both. Fix: quotePosixCommandArg single-quotes an argument holding !, CR or LF, or ending in a backslash; every other spelling is unchanged."}]}],"before_hash":"2f9e736cd42ac95922e631b41a9deccf87f7e2c1a07bc53e6067e640ccd35b52","after_hash":"a6a928889c56fc375fd0681224d02d080a0574eea7dae71b55963c280da35417","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f943fe6332a8d7ed733ff330d64a3cc26b3be9d9b5e36ad8d107d3b5363b328e"}
